# v0.1.3 item 1 — SKILL.md packages bundle

2026-05-04. v0.1.3 item per `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-x-roadmap.md`
§2 v0.1.3 item 1 + Decision D (ship 5 packages) + §8
method-decision register backfill.

Sub-plan: `docs/rebuild/plans/v0-1-3-skill-packages.md`.

FIDRAFT entry closed (`docs/rebuild/FUTURE_IDEAS_DRAFT.md` —
captured 2026-05-03):
  - "Anthropic-perspective recommendation ladder (R.1-R.6)" —
    item R.4 (3-5 SKILL.md packages) lands here.

Scope (per sub-plan §5): single-component fence on the NEW
plugin `plugins/loam-skills/`. Second sealed component under
the `plugins/` tree (first was `dev-sdlc` at v0.1.0 M6a). Leaf
plugin — markdown-only artefact, no runtime dependencies, no
`loam.bootstrap.contributions` entry-point. Skills are
filesystem-discovered by Claude Code natively per Anthropic's
SKILL.md schema (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills).

Three AC families (all under AC.LSK.*):

  - AC.LSK.1 — five SKILL.md packages present and well-formed.
    Each file: starts with valid YAML frontmatter delimited
    by `---`; frontmatter parses as mapping; carries non-empty
    `description` field (≤1536 chars per Anthropic's combined
    cap); body (post-frontmatter) is non-empty markdown.

  - AC.LSK.2 — frontmatter follows Anthropic SKILL.md schema.
    Directory name kebab-case + ≤64 chars. If `name` field
    present, matches directory name. Description carries
    trigger-phrase clause ("use when" / "before" / "when X").
    No unknown frontmatter fields beyond `name` (optional)
    and `description` — minimal v0.1.3 surface.

  - AC.LSK.3 — body content shape. Required sections:
    `## What this skill captures`, `## When to use`,
    `## How the persona applies it`, `## Graceful degradation`,
    `## Composition`, `## Out of scope`. Body references at
    least one named loam pattern (F3, F4, ODD, M-FBM, FIDRAFT,
    Lens 1, etc.) for traceable provenance. Graceful-degradation
    section names raw-Claude-Code path explicitly.

  - AC.LSK.S — single-component fence on `plugins/loam-skills/`;
    plus `docs/rebuild/plans/` via universal prefix; plus
    `install-from-source.txt` + `docs/install-from-source.md`
    via component-level `extra_allowed_files` (Tier K append).

The 5 SKILL.md packages (per Decision D — ship 5):

  1. memory-recall — file-based memory retrieval pattern.
     Composes with M-FBM's auto-injected per-turn retrieval
     block; degrades to filesystem search for raw Claude Code.
  2. scope-decompose — F3 swarming stopping criterion.
     "Decompose if subtasks have tighter ACs; stop when split
     adds only coordination overhead."
  3. dispatch-with-gates — scope-only dispatch + halt-and-surface.
     "Pass objective + scope + constraints + halt triggers +
     ODD-check ONLY. Never enumerate files / symbols / ACs."
  4. onboarding-conversation — primary-persona greeting shape
     for fresh sessions. Surfaces what's in flight + what
     needs attention + what just completed.
  5. session-handoff — durable-capture rule before session
     close. "Files are the only memory; nothing is session-
     locked."

