All ACs (AC.LSK.{1,2,3}) pass: 5 SKILL.md files exist with
well-formed frontmatter + standard body shape + named loam-
pattern provenance + graceful-degradation guidance for raw
Claude Code.

Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - Frontmatter minimalism: only `description` (Anthropic's
    recommended minimum). `name` defaults to directory name.
    No `disable-model-invocation`, `allowed-tools`, etc — these
    are reference-content skills (knowledge applied alongside
    conversation), not task-shaped skills with side effects.
  - Body section shape mirrors existing flat-skill convention
    (`memory-search.md`, `start-project.md`) plus an explicit
    `## Graceful degradation` section so raw-Claude-Code users
    know what to do when loam infrastructure isn't present.
  - Plugin pyproject.toml has NO `loam.bootstrap.contributions`
    entry-point — skills are filesystem-discovered by Claude
    Code natively per the Anthropic schema. The pyproject
    exists solely so `pip install -e ./plugins/loam-skills`
    recognises the package.
  - Plugin is markdown-only — no Python source modules.
    `setuptools.packages = []` keeps auto-discovery from
    creating spurious top-level modules.
  - Test files mirror AC.LAE.* shape from v0.1.2 item 6
    (parametrized tests, AC-named modules, sealed-component
    partner test_no_sealed_amendments.py).
  - Tier K append in install-from-source.txt (one-line entry)
    + corresponding update in docs/install-from-source.md
    (per-component fallback section). Both admitted via
    component-level `extra_allowed_files` since they sit
    outside the plugin's subtree.

Out of scope (per sub-plan §9):

  - Migration of existing flat-shape skills
    (plugins/dev-sdlc/skills/start-project.md +
    framework/primary-persona/skills/memory-{search,archive}.md)
    to the modern directory-per-skill shape — out of fence;
    v0.2+ if Anthropic discovery requires it.
  - Live `claude` binary discovery smoke (boot-claude-in-fixture)
    — out of fence; static-walk smoke is sufficient at the
    amendment-cycle level.
  - Updating dev-mode-manifest.yaml for plugins/loam-skills/
    — `roots:` doesn't include plugins/* by default; same
    treatment as plugins/dev-sdlc/. Follow-on amendment if
    dev-mode loading wants to surface to the persona.
  - PyPI publishing — deferred to v0.2 per the broader publish
    gate.
  - A 6th SKILL package or beyond — Decision D locks at 5.
  - Reference scripts in the SKILL packages — none in v0.1.3;
    all 5 are pure markdown reference content. Can extend in
    v0.1.4+ if specific patterns benefit.

